-- title:
--   p-torsion of the Dieudonné module lies in L+ker V
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime (as a `Fact`), let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring in which the image of $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, and let $k$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra whose structure map $\mathcal O \to k$ is surjective with kernel exactly the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-bialgebra which is flat as an $\mathcal O$-module, and put $A = k \otimes_{\mathcal O} \mathcal R$ with its induced $k$-bialgebra structure. Here [`Deformation.DieudonneModule k p A`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234) is the direct limit, along the maps induced by the shift `wittHomShiftLE`, of the additive subgroups [`Deformation.wittHom k p n A`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246) of truncated Witt vectors $x \in W_n(A)$ satisfying $\Delta_* x = (\iota_1)_* x + (\iota_2)_* x$ for the comultiplication of $A$ and the two inclusions $A \to A \otimes_k A$; [`Deformation.fontaineHodge k p \pi`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) is the subgroup (as a $\mathbb Z$-submodule) of classes represented by some $x \in$ `wittHom k p n A` whose underlying truncated Witt vector lies in [`Deformation.TruncWitt.fontaineKer p n \pi`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L76); and `verschiebung` is the endomorphism of the limit induced levelwise by the Verschiebung of truncated Witt vectors. The assertion: for every $z$ in this Dieudonné module with $(p : \mathbb Z) \cdot z = 0$, there are $y$ in `fontaineHodge k p` of the reduction map $\mathcal R \to A$, $r \mapsto 1 \otimes r$ (the ring homomorphism underlying `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight`), and $x$ in the Dieudonné module with $V x = 0$, such that $y + x = z$.
--
--   This is the inclusion $M[p] \subseteq L + \ker V$ in Fontaine's analysis of the Dieudonné module $M$ of the special fibre of a finite flat commutative group scheme, with $L$ the submodule cut out by Fontaine's map; only the existence of a decomposition is asserted, not its directness. It is used in the comparison of $L$ with $M$ that yields [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_hondaSystem_L_eq_fontaineHodge`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_hondaSystem_L_eq_fontaineHodge).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_exists_mem_fontaineHodge_add_eq_of_smul_eq_zero.lean

